        "calls": 2,
        "title": "Ad engagement end reason drops unknown values and adds expired",
        "summary": "The ad engagement record in `common/src/types/ad-client-context.ts` adds `expired` to the `ENGAGEMENT_ENDED_BY` vocabulary, indicating an ad was taken off screen due to a wall-clock cap or away-time limit. The `endedBy` field now applies `.catch(undefined)` so that an unrecognized end reason is dropped from the record rather than causing the entire engagement record to fail parsing. This additive change allows newer clients to send the `expired` value before older servers that do not yet recognize it are updated, preserving the rest of the timing data in the record.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "advertisers",
        "evidence": "In `common/src/types/ad-client-context.ts`, the `ENGAGEMENT_ENDED_BY` array gained a new `'expired'` value, and the `endedBy` field in `adEngagementSchema` was changed from a strict enum to one with `.catch(undefined)` to drop unknown values.",
        "userVisible": false,
        "confidence": "medium",
