      "facts": [
        "A local Codex chat saves the same marks (Desktop's codex.ts): `session` is its Codex thread and `end` the run's last native turn, which a rollback forks the thread through (`thread/fork` with `lastTurnId`).",
        "A Claude Code chat's wake (the kept process answered on its own after a background task finished): the turn sends nothing and shows that answer (Desktop's claude-live-session.ts). Cloud queues one only for a Desktop that reported the wake, so no older build sees it.",
        "Queued by the chat's Desktop when its Claude Code process answered on its own after a background task finished (web device-execution/background-wake.ts): no message opens it. Absent from older servers.",
        "Finished tasks the Overview still lists: the most recent ones, for a while after they end.",
        "A Claude Code or Codex process is kept for this chat; false means nothing can be running in it.",
        "Task ids are the CLI's own (Codex: a subagent's thread id, a command's item id); anything else is refused before it reaches a process."
